21:- **Whole code units, best first.** Results are ranked, with functions, classes and methods ahead of imports and re-exports. A search for `format price` puts `formatCurrency` and `validatePrice` first, because names are split on `camelCase`, `snake_case` and acronyms before matching.
58:Each row is one match: where it is (`file`, `lineStart`, `lineEnd`), what it is (`nodeKind`: function, class, interface, type alias and so on), its signature, the lines in it that matched (`snippet`), and its `rank` and `finalScore`. Output uses [TOON](https://github.com/toon-format/spec), a table format that costs fewer tokens than JSON.

